variant: instructional-explanatory-figure
references:
- references/fim/overview/geospatial-math-scientific/mathbox.md
- references/fim/solution/mathbox.md
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior 3D math education engineer. Output only one complete ASCII HTML file using MathBox. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create an instructional MathBox figure explaining spherical coordinates. Show axes, a unit sphere wireframe, a point P, radius vector r, projected radius on the xy-plane, angle theta around z, angle phi from the positive z-axis, and sliders or controls that move theta and phi.

    Requirements: use cartesian or spherical views, array/interval data for vectors and arcs, labels or HTML overlays for r, theta, phi, x, y, z, and a step explanation panel. Provide non-color encodings for vectors and arcs and keep the camera framed at first render.
  provider_options:
    temperature: 0.2
    max_tokens: 8192
output:
  text_format: html
  artifact_kind: mathbox-html
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: png
  - format: webgl
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present."
  - "HTML is complete, ASCII-only, and uses MathBox primitives for vectors, arcs, sphere, labels, and controls."
  - "Math correctness covers spherical-coordinate definitions, projections, angle ranges, and point coordinates."
  - "Notation validity covers theta, phi, r labels, axis labels, units in radians, and explanatory steps."
  - "Renderability covers nonblank first frame, controls, camera framing, and WebGL fallback status."
  - "Labels and units identify r, theta, phi, x, y, z, projected radius, point P, and unit sphere."
  - "Domain edge cases cover theta wraparound, phi endpoints, overlapping labels, resize, and color-only encodings."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII HTML file with no Markdown wrapper."
    - "The file uses valid MathBox and JavaScript controls."
    - "The source documents dependency, run, fallback, and capture behavior."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Sphere, axes, point, radius vector, projection, angle arcs, controls, labels, and steps are all present."
    - "MathBox is used for the 3D instructional visualization."
    - "Coordinate formulas and visible geometry agree."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "The 3D scene is clean, framed, and readable immediately."
    - "Angles, vectors, and projections are distinguishable without color alone."
    - "Controls and explanations do not occlude the scene."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles angle endpoints, wraparound, resize, and label overlap."
    - "Uses stable controls and bounded updates."
    - "Documents WebGL, device, and capture constraints."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in math correctness, notation validity, renderability, or accessibility."
  - "The artifact teaches spherical coordinates through a visible interactive MathBox scene."
  - "Labels, units, domain edge cases, and accessibility considerations are represented."
